# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Keep the reusable framework tracked; keep everything specific to
# YOUR league, your analysis, your data, and your secrets LOCAL.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Your local config (briefing, secrets) — keep everything except the templates/README ──
/config/*
!/config/*.example
!/config/*.example.*
!/config/README.md
# …and the curated Tier-B research allow-list: reusable, not league-specific (WS-2).
!/config/research_sources.json

# ── Secrets & credentials ──
**/.env
**/.env.local
!**/.env.example
scraping/.espn_auth.json
*.pem

# ── Scraped league data (re-generate from your own ESPN account) ──
scraping/raw/
scraping/har_extracted/
*.har

# ── Projection sheets & derived data (source-specific / copyrighted) ──
draft_sheets/*.xlsm
draft_sheets/*.xlsx
draft_sheets/*.csv
# …but DO track the universal Elboberto baseline projections workbook (checked in):
!draft_sheets/*_elboberto.xlsm
draft_sheets/elboberto_projections.json
draft_sheets/tool_data.json

# ── Generated app payload (built by the inject step from the template) ──
draft_app/static/index.html
draft_app/static/data.json
# ── Generated launcher + per-league in-season cockpits (inject_season.py) ──
draft_app/static/home.html
draft_app/static/leagues.json
draft_app/static/l/
draft_sheets/out/

# ── Analysis: the pipeline CODE is tracked; league-specific identity lives in
#    config/ (manager_canon.json / league.json). Only the ANALYSIS OUTPUTS and
#    private notes stay local. ──
reports/
league/
draft_app/eval_report.md

# ── Python env & caches ──
.venv/
venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ── Local tooling / scratch / OS ──
.claude/
.playwright-mcp/
review-*.png
.DS_Store

# CSG sheet (third-party) + its extracted consensus data — local only
draft_sheets/csg_consensus.json

# ── In-season generated payloads (built by the season-* / data-console stages) ──
draft_app/static/home.html
draft_app/static/l/
draft_app/static/data_console*.html
draft_app/static/data_console*.json
draft_sheets/out/

# ── Working docs + fixtures built from YOUR leagues ──
# Same rule as reports/: the reusable CODE is tracked, anything naming your leagues,
# their ids, managers or team names stays local. tests/fixtures/ is regenerated by
# `python3 tests/make_fixture.py`.
#
# docs/ is SPLIT, because two different things were living in one directory:
#   docs/*.md      the engineering contracts future work must follow — tracked, and
#                  therefore kept free of league ids, manager names and team names.
#                  Adding a doc here is a decision to publish it: the remote is public.
#   docs/local/    plans, the PM board and the per-workstream wiring sheets. These name
#                  real leagues (inseason_plan.md carries all three league ids and team
#                  names), and they are build-time scaffolding rather than a contract.
docs/local/
tests/fixtures/
